{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>For completely closed… on account of the matter of…</b> The meaning is that they should not say Sarah conceived from Avimelech — for he was sterile in those days. And also to reveal that the prayer of Abraham is effective to remember barren women, and it was effective even for himself, and he was remembered. Also to make known: all who pray on behalf of another and he himself has the same need, etc., he is answered, etc. And therefore Scripture juxtaposed to this verse the verse ״וַה׳ פָּקַד אֶת שָׂרָה״. And although the promise had already preceded, if the matter of juxtaposition does not apply to the thing itself, assign it to another matter, and see the comment on the verse that follows this one:"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:33.964393422Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}